course: dictionary
lesson: 12931
title: Eventual: the end of the road
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Eventual means final, the thing that happens at the very end, after a long time or a series of steps. When you meet it, look for clues about time, such as after many rounds, at last or in the end. «The eventual winner of the spelling bee was Maya, who had beaten everyone in the earlier rounds.» There were many rounds, and Maya won at the end, so eventual means final.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «the final winner» instead of «the eventual winner». It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Eventual often goes with words like success, outcome and result. «Her eventual success came after three years of practice.» The success arrived at the end, not at the start. «The eventual outcome of the story surprised everyone» means how things finally turned out.
fact: Eventual is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «the eventual winner».
fact: «Eventual» means happening at the end of a long time or after a series of events; final.
fact: «Eventual» is close in meaning to «final», but it often points back to a long wait or many steps.
fact: «Eventual success» means success that came in the end, after effort.
fact: Time clues such as after, at last and in the end often show that eventual is the right meaning.
exercise: «The eventual winner of the spelling bee was Maya, who had beaten everyone in the earlier rounds.» What does eventual mean here? | Loudest, the one who shouted most | *Final, the one who won at the end | First, the one who started quickest | Youngest, the smallest in the class
exercise: «Her eventual success came after three years of practice.» What does eventual success mean? | A small prize for trying | Success that came right at the start | *Success that came in the end, after effort | Success that nobody noticed
exercise: Grandad asks, «What was the eventual outcome of the match?» What is he asking? | Why the match was cancelled | What the score was at half time | Who arrived first at the ground | *How the match finally ended
test: After many rounds of voting, «the eventual choice of class captain» was Sam. What does eventual mean here? | Angry, made with shouting | Secret, nobody knew about it | *Final, the choice made at the end | Quick, made in one second
test: In «the eventual result», which word could replace eventual and keep the meaning? | Hungry | *Final | Sudden | Dark
exam: «The eventual outcome of the experiment was clear after six weeks.» Eventual means: | *Happening at the end, final | Happening at the very start | Happening in secret, where nobody can see | Happening every single day
